DTRACE COVERAGE: TENTH EXPANSION
===============================

Twenty additional base utility components; 44 new USDT contracts and ten
base-install profiles. This round is userland only and complements the
kernel, bhyve, Bluetooth, Mesh, MACF and library coverage in earlier rounds.
It does not claim complete coverage of these utilities or of the system.

Selection and history
---------------------
The new runtime source files do not overlap the eighth or ninth rounds.
Reviewed recent history includes 43b0384bc7e (mountpoint as a stat hardlink),
fe06e383cc6 (daemon pidfile without supervision), and 2c88636e0e7 (stat tests).
Stat/readlink/mountpoint share one executable: metadata lookups are traced,
not every readlink operation. Daemon probes cover actual event registration
and waits; the non-supervising execution path need not produce these probes.

Twenty passes and precise scope
-------------------------------
 1. usr.bin/touch (filetime*): Each timestamp update, including retry; flags, result and errno. No timestamps or paths.
 2. usr.bin/stat (filestat*): Metadata queries: kind 0 stat, 1 lstat, 2 fstat. Result/errno; excludes fhstat and readlink payload.
 3. usr.sbin/chown (fileowner*): Ownership update attempts, including chgrp alias; flags and result, no identities/paths.
 4. usr.bin/mkfifo (fifocreate*): FIFO creation mode, result and errno.
 5. usr.bin/pathchk (pathcheck*): Filesystem-aware path component lookup; ENOENT may be accepted by the caller, not a command failure.
 6. usr.bin/du (diskwalk*): One traversal advance; result is FTS entry type, zero is end/error; terminal errno distinguishes those. Entry-specific errors remain in fts_errno.
 7. bin/df (diskspace*): Per-path filesystem usage query; excludes bulk getmntinfo.
 8. sbin/sysctl (sysctltool*): Sysctl query/set and name-walking requests; write flag and MIB length, never values or MIB buffers.
 9. usr.bin/limits (limittool*): Current-process resource limit application; resource/result; excludes target-process sysctl mode.
10. usr.bin/killall (signalall*): Each selected-process signal attempt; pid, signal, result, errno. Dry-run produces no send probes.
11. bin/kill (signaltool*): Numeric signal syscall boundary including signal-zero checks; no process names.
12. usr.bin/logger (logsend*): Remote datagram send length, bytes/result and errno; local submission pair is void and does not claim delivery.
13. usr.sbin/daemon (daemonwait*): Supervisor event registration and waits; change/event capacities, returned count and errno. No probes in signal handlers.
14. usr.bin/env (envdir*): Requested working-directory change before exec; no environment or command values.
15. usr.bin/getconf (configquery*): Sysconf query key and returned value; -1 with errno zero is indeterminate, not a failure.
16. bin/cpuset (cpusettool*): Affinity read/write operation kind, level and selector; no masks. Excludes domain/id operations.
17. bin/timeout (timeoutsig*): Foreground signal dispatch including SIGCONT; reaper dispatch has its own pair. Signal handlers only set flags.
18. bin/realpath (pathresolve*): Path resolution boundary; boolean success and errno, no input/resolved strings.
19. bin/sleep (sleepwait*): Each sleep attempt, completion and interruption; duration measured by paired timestamps outside signal handler.
20. usr.bin/mktemp (tempcreate*): Temporary file (kind 0) or directory (kind 1) creation; boolean success/errno, never templates or generated paths.

Probe contracts
---------------
All selectors use provider*:::name. Types and argument order below are the
public contract. An operation-done repeats the start arguments, followed by
result and errno. Errno is zero on success; syscall result -1 indicates
failure, except sysconf's indeterminate -1/errno-zero result. Pointer-return
APIs expose scalar outcomes only. No command strings, paths, environment
variables, messages, credentials, CPU masks or sysctl values are collected.

